First, based on the provided triplets, we can see that multiple units are part of the International System of Units (SI) for measuring length. These include Millimeter, Picometre, Micrometer, Decimetre, Kilometer, Centimeter, Nanometre, Hectometre, Megametre, Decametre, Meter.

To provide a concise answer to how the International System of Units measures length, we can combine these units into a coherent statement. The International System of Units uses various standardized units such as meter (m), centimeter (cm), millimeter (mm), and their prefixes like kilo (k), hecto (h), deca (da), deci (d), and so on, to measure length. Each prefix modifies the base unit (meter) by a factor of 10.

So, the answer is {The International System of Units measures length using standardized units such as meter (m), centimeter (cm), millimeter (mm), kilometer (km), hectometer (hm), decameter (dam), and their respective prefixes for different scales.}
